<p class="tagline">Document scanner</p>
<span class="badge">🔒 No account, no tracking, no internet required</span>

<h1 style="margin-top:36px;">Privacy Policy</h1>
<p>Scanolio is a document scanning app. It does not ask you to create an account or provide any personal information, and it does not send your documents anywhere.</p>

<div class="emoji">📷</div>
<h2>Camera access</h2>
<p>Scanolio uses your camera only to scan documents. Photos are captured, corner-detected, and processed entirely on your device using on-device machine learning — nothing is uploaded to a server for this.</p>

<div class="emoji">💾</div>
<h2>Where your scans are stored</h2>
<p>Scanned documents, page images, and folder organization are stored locally in the app's private storage on your device. Nothing is sent to us or to any third-party server. If you uninstall the app, this data is deleted along with it.</p>

<div class="emoji">🚫</div>
<h2>We collect zero personal data</h2>
<p>Scanolio does not collect, store, or transmit any personal data. There is no account, no login, and no user profile of any kind.</p>

<div class="emoji">📤</div>
<h2>Sharing your documents</h2>
<p>When you choose to share a scan as a PDF, Scanolio hands it to Android's built-in share sheet — you pick where it goes (email, messaging apps, cloud storage, etc.). We don't see or handle that transfer, and the app doesn't send it anywhere on its own.</p>

<div class="emoji">🚷</div>
<h2>What we never do</h2>
<ul>
  <li>No account or login required</li>
  <li>No data sold or shared with third parties</li>
  <li>No access to contacts, location, or microphone</li>
</ul>

<div class="emoji">🔄</div>
<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
<p>If Scanolio ever adds a feature that changes how data is handled (for example, optional cloud backup), this page will be updated first and the update will be reflected in the app.</p>

